in \code{anova_groups} — by default just \code{"taxon"}, the grouping column that
\code{\link[=morph_matrix_setting]{morph_matrix_setting()}} always attaches. Passing any other name only
works if that column has been added to \code{analysis_data} beforehand (e.g. a
locality or growth-form column merged in before calling this function);
\code{morph_anova()} does not read from any other object.

The \code{anova_blocks} argument controls which trait sets are analyzed:

\itemize{
\item \code{"all"}: runs ANOVA on each individual block in \code{base_cols}
(typically \code{"veg"}, \code{"flo"}, \code{"fru"}), as well as on every pairwise and
full combination of these blocks (\code{"vegflo"}, \code{"vegfru"}, \code{"flofru"},
\code{"vegflofru"}). Combinations whose source blocks are absent from
\code{base_cols} are silently skipped;
\item a character vector naming one or more blocks in \code{base_cols}: runs
ANOVA only on the requested block(s), individually.
